; SLP passes the cost query only the first lane's address, so the target cannot
; tell a shared base from a varying one. It is shared exactly when every pointer
; is a GEP off the same operand, which is the form that widens to one base plus
; a vector of indices.
;
; Guessing from that one address gets both shapes below wrong, and in opposite
; directions. The shared base here is an instruction and the varying one is an
; argument.

; RUN: opt < %s -S -passes=slp-vectorizer -mtriple=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu \
; RUN:   -mcpu=skylake | FileCheck %s

